  <ferc:VendorName id="f-536" contextRef="c-1">The Workiva Platform</ferc:VendorName>
  <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-1" id="fn-1" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Refer to Note 4 &#8212; Long-Term Debt &amp; Derivative Instruments for additional disclosure.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1986, by its Section 3401(a)(1), requires the Commission to assess and collect fees and annual charges in any fiscal year in amounts equal to all of the costs incurred by the Commission in a fiscal year. For the purposes of recovering this payment, this Section establishes a FERC ACA Unit Charge to be applicable to all jurisdictional transportation quantities transported. These costs will continue to be recovered under its current rates with customers.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ASC 740 considers the equity component of AFUDC a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes must be provided. The Respondent is required to record the deferred tax liability for AFUDC equity in Account 282 with a corresponding regulatory asset. The regulatory asset is itself a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes are recognized and recorded in Account 283. This accounting is also outlined in FERC Docket AI93-5-000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This balance represents the impact of U.S. Tax Reform as applied to businesses subject to rate-regulated accounting. The regulatory liability will be amortized over varying terms that approximate the expected reversal of the underlying deferred tax assets and liabilities that gave rise to the regulatory liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Gas Uses include, but are not limited to, Flow Tests, Blowing Drips, Running Pigs/Spheres, RemovingFreezes, Blowing Down Lines, Well Construction, Compressor Station Blowdowns, Consumer Taps, Methanol LineInstallation, and increases in customer storage.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Receipts include decreases in customer storage.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Hardy customers only pay ACA on injections; therefore, amounts withdrawn from storage are excluded for ACA calculation purposes. Volume to be used for ACA calculation year to date 2025 is 12,455,762 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Hardy Storage Company's contract storage quantity at 3/31/2026 was 12,361,000 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accounts debited include 817,818,823,825.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent has a Commission approved Retainage Adjustment Mechanism (RAM) that recovers from shippers system gas used and lost. Any excess or deficient balance is included in the next annual filing and collected or passed back to customers as appropriate through a change in the surcharge to newly established rates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Storage injections and withdrawals are excluded as associated DTH's do not represent throughput.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent uses a monthly average spot rate as the basis for valuing gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Hardy customers only pay ACA on injections; therefore, amounts withdrawn from storage are excluded for ACA calculation purposes. Volume to be used for ACA calculation year to date 2025 is 12,455,762&#160; Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Refer to Note 4 &#8212; Long-Term Debt &amp; Derivative Instruments in the Notes to Financial Statements pg. 122 for more detail on the Term Loan refinancing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Hardy customers only pay ACA on injections; therefore, amounts withdrawn from storage are excluded for ACAcalculation purposes. Volume to be used for ACA calculation for 2025 is 12,455,762 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">These costs are based on direct assignment to the extent practicable, or by using allocation methods that are reasonable reflections of the utilization of services provided to or for the benefits received by the Company.</link:footnote>
